# Sources: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/
# and fisher-l7f owner decisions from 2026-11-22.
# Search: fisher-2aj rules 1, 4, 9 and 10, with owner-approved terminal replies
# based on the Stockfish examples cited in fisher-2aj.2.
# Searched transcript written 2026-11-23.
> position fen 7k/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
> go infinite
# Rule 9 sends info before the reply to isready. The move waits for stop.
# The owner approved this line on 2026-11-23 in a comment on fisher-2aj.2.
# The ticket cites Stockfish as a witness for stalemate.
# This line departs from rule 10 by omitting the node count and from
# rule 1 by reporting depth 0 instead of 4.
< info depth 0 score cp 0
> isready
# UCI go infinite and isready. No bestmove precedes readyok.
< readyok
> stop
# UCI stop/bestmove releases the held move for stalemate, 0000.
< bestmove 0000
# UCI quit.
> quit
! exit
